| `scribe/src/operations.rs` | `ensure_layer_exists` + all 6 handlers: use units |
| `scribe/src/loro_observer.rs` | `setup_layer_observer` + `setup_observers_for_all_layers`: use units, capture `is_local_only` as bool |
| `scribe/src/sync/mod.rs` | `handle_flush`, sync request handlers: use units |
| `scribe/src/sync/apply.rs` | `UpdateContext::new`, `create_layer_from_peer`, `apply_crdt_update`, `update_sender_vector`, `handle_post_apply`: use units |
| `scribe/src/sync/broadcast.rs` | `broadcast_update`, `notify_layer_discovered`: use units |
| `scribe/src/sync/reconcile.rs` | `handle_reconcile_with_peers`: iterate units |
| `scribe/src/sync/subscription.rs` | `send_initial_state_to_subscriber`: iterate units |
| `scribe/src/query.rs` | `handle_query`: use units |
| `scribe/src/permit.rs` | No changes (delegates to gurkha) |
| `scribe/src/layer_unit/dynamic.rs` | Use `state.units` instead of `state.layers` |
| `scribe/src/ephemeral.rs` | No changes (doesn't access layers) |

## Mechanical Transformation Rules

Every access site follows one of these patterns:

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| `state.layers.get(name)` | `state.units.get(name).map(\|u\| u.layer())` |
| `state.layers.get_mut(name)` | `state.units.get_mut(name).map(\|u\| u.layer())` |
| `state.layers.contains_key(name)` | `state.units.contains_key(name)` |
| `state.layers.insert(name, Layer::new())` | `state.units.insert(name, LayerUnit::new_empty())` |
| `state.layers.insert(name, layer)` | `state.units.insert(name, LayerUnit::new(layer))` |
| `state.layers.keys()` | `state.units.keys()` |
| `state.layers.entry(name).or_insert_with(Layer::new)` | Unit entry pattern (see below) |
| `state.dirty_layers.insert(name)` | `state.units.get_mut(name).unwrap().mark_dirty()` |
| `state.dirty_layers.drain()` | iterate `units.iter_mut()`, check `take_dirty_snapshot()` |
| `state.dirty_layers.is_empty()` | `state.units.values().all(\|u\| !u.is_dirty())` |
| `state.dirty_layers.remove(name)` | `state.units.get_mut(name).map(\|u\| u.clear_dirty())` |
| `state.loro_subscriptions.contains_key(name)` | `state.units.get(name).map(\|u\| u.has_observer()).unwrap_or(false)` |
| `state.loro_subscriptions.insert(name, sub)` | `state.units.get_mut(name).unwrap().set_observer(sub)` |
| `state.loro_subscriptions.len()` | `state.units.values().filter(\|u\| u.has_observer()).count()` |
| `state.local_only_layers` (all refs) | Removed — use `unit.is_local_only()` |
| `state.mark_layer_local_only_if_needed(name)` | `unit.set_local_only(!state.should_sync_layer(name))` |

**Entry pattern** (used in `handle_update_from_json`):
```rust
// Before:
let layer = state.layers.entry(name).or_insert_with(Layer::new);
// After:
let unit = state.units.entry(name).or_insert_with(LayerUnit::new_empty);
let layer = unit.layer();
```

## Implementation Order

### Step 1: Create LayerUnit struct
Add `LayerUnit` to `scribe/src/layer_unit/mod.rs` with all methods.

### Step 2: Update ScribeState
Replace 4 collections with `units: HashMap<String, LayerUnit>`. Remove helper methods. Keep `should_sync_layer()`.

### Step 3: Update pre_start (actor.rs)
Convert `args.layers` → units in `pre_start`. Set `is_local_only` on each unit. Remove `update_local_only_layers()` call.

### Step 4: Update loro_observer.rs
Change `setup_layer_observer` + `setup_observers_for_all_layers` to use units. Capture `is_local_only` as bool.

### Step 5: Update operations.rs
Change `ensure_layer_exists` + all 6 operation handlers to use units.

### Step 6: Update sync/ modules
- `sync/mod.rs`: flush, sync request handlers
- `sync/apply.rs`: UpdateContext, create_layer_from_peer, apply_crdt_update, etc.
- `sync/broadcast.rs`: broadcast_update, notify_layer_discovered
- `sync/reconcile.rs`: handle_reconcile_with_peers
- `sync/subscription.rs`: send_initial_state_to_subscriber

### Step 7: Update actor.rs message handlers
All remaining `state.layers.get()` / `state.dirty_layers.insert()` etc. in handle().

### Step 8: Update remaining modules
- `query.rs`: state.layers.get → state.units.get
- `layer_unit/dynamic.rs`: state.layers → state.units

### Step 9: Compile + test
Fix all compilation errors. Run existing tests.

## Unit Tests

### LayerUnit struct tests (`scribe/src/layer_unit/mod.rs`)

```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use domains::Layer;

    #[test]
    fn test_new_empty() {
        let unit = LayerUnit::new_empty();
        assert!(!unit.is_dirty());
        assert!(!unit.is_local_only());
        assert!(!unit.is_dynamic());
        assert!(!unit.has_observer());
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_new_with_layer() {
        let layer = Layer::new();
        let map = layer.loro().get_map("test");
        map.insert("key", "value").unwrap();
        layer.commit();

        let unit = LayerUnit::new(layer);
        // Layer data preserved
        let content = unit.layer().to_json();
        assert!(content.get("test").is_some());
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_dirty_tracking() {
        let mut unit = LayerUnit::new_empty();
        assert!(!unit.is_dirty());
        assert!(unit.take_dirty_snapshot().is_none());

        unit.mark_dirty();
        assert!(unit.is_dirty());

        let snapshot = unit.take_dirty_snapshot();
        assert!(snapshot.is_some());
        // Flag cleared after take
        assert!(!unit.is_dirty());
        assert!(unit.take_dirty_snapshot().is_none());
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_dirty_snapshot_contains_data() {
        let mut unit = LayerUnit::new_empty();
        let list = unit.layer().loro().get_list("items");
        list.push("hello").unwrap();
        unit.layer().commit();
        unit.mark_dirty();

        let snapshot = unit.take_dirty_snapshot().unwrap();
        // Snapshot can be used to reconstruct layer
        let restored = Layer::from_snapshot(&snapshot).unwrap();
        let content = restored.to_json();
        assert!(content.get("items").is_some());
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_local_only_flag() {
        let mut unit = LayerUnit::new_empty();
        assert!(!unit.is_local_only());

        unit.set_local_only(true);
        assert!(unit.is_local_only());

        unit.set_local_only(false);
        assert!(!unit.is_local_only());
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_dynamic_flag() {
        let mut unit = LayerUnit::new_empty();
        assert!(!unit.is_dynamic());

        unit.is_dynamic = true;
        assert!(unit.is_dynamic());
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_observer_lifecycle() {
        let mut unit = LayerUnit::new_empty();
        assert!(!unit.has_observer());

        // Create a real Loro subscription
        let sub = unit.layer().subscribe_root(|_| {});
        unit.set_observer(sub);
        assert!(unit.has_observer());

        unit.clear_observer();
        assert!(!unit.has_observer());
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_clear_dirty() {
        let mut unit = LayerUnit::new_empty();
        unit.mark_dirty();
        assert!(unit.is_dirty());

        unit.clear_dirty();
        assert!(!unit.is_dirty());
    }
}
```

### Existing test impact

The existing Scribe tests (`actor.rs::tests`, `layer_unit/dynamic.rs::tests`) access ScribeState internally. Changes:

- `actor.rs::test_ephemeral_with_no_subscribers` — uses `node_scribe_args()` which returns `ScribeArgs` with `layers: HashMap<String, Layer>`. This stays unchanged since `pre_start` handles the conversion.
- `layer_unit/dynamic.rs::test_generate_dynamic_path` — pure function, no state access. Unchanged.
- `layer_unit/dynamic.rs::test_validate_creator_namespace` — pure function. Unchanged.
- `layer_unit/dynamic.rs::test_prepare_layer_permits_*` — uses `NullPermitIssuer`, no state. Unchanged.
- `permit.rs::tests` — uses `gurkha::matches_wildcard`, no state. Unchanged.
- `test_fixtures.rs::node_scribe_args()` — creates `ScribeArgs`. Check if it sets `layers` field; if so, no change needed (pre_start converts).

## Verification

```bash
