    25→    layer: Layer,
    26→    /// Needs flush to storage?
    27→    dirty: bool,
    28→    /// sync: false in permit — never broadcast
    29→    is_local_only: bool,
    30→    /// Created via dynamic_layer_schema (not static template)
    31→    is_dynamic: bool,
    32→    /// Loro observer subscription (dropped = unsubscribed)
    33→    loro_sub: Option<loro::Subscription>,
    34→}
    35→```
    36→
    37→Key: Layer is `Clone` (confirmed at `loro_observer.rs:320`), so observer tasks get their own clone.
    38→
    39→### LayerUnit API
    40→
    41→```rust
    42→impl LayerUnit {
    43→    pub fn new(layer: Layer) -> Self;
    44→    pub fn new_empty() -> Self;      // Layer::new()
    45→
    46→    // Layer access
    47→    pub fn layer(&self) -> &Layer;
    48→    pub fn layer_mut(&mut self) -> &mut Layer;  // for in-place ops if needed
    49→
    50→    // Dirty tracking
    51→    pub fn mark_dirty(&mut self);
    52→    pub fn is_dirty(&self) -> bool;
    53→    /// Export snapshot if dirty, clear flag. Returns None if clean.
    54→    pub fn take_dirty_snapshot(&mut self) -> Option<Vec<u8>>;
    55→
    56→    // Metadata
    57→    pub fn is_local_only(&self) -> bool;
    58→    pub fn set_local_only(&mut self, val: bool);
    59→    pub fn is_dynamic(&self) -> bool;
    60→
    61→    // Observer lifecycle
    62→    pub fn has_observer(&self) -> bool;
    63→    pub fn set_observer(&mut self, sub: loro::Subscription);
    64→    /// Drop the observer (unsubscribes from Loro)
    65→    pub fn clear_observer(&mut self);
    66→}
    67→```
    68→
    69→### ScribeState Changes
    70→
    71→**Remove**:
    72→- `layers: HashMap<String, Layer>`
    73→- `dirty_layers: HashSet<String>`
    74→- `loro_subscriptions: HashMap<String, loro::Subscription>`
    75→- `local_only_layers: Arc<RwLock<HashSet<String>>>`
    76→
    77→**Add**:
    78→- `units: HashMap<String, LayerUnit>`
    79→
    80→**Remove methods**:
    81→- `update_local_only_layers()` — replaced by per-unit flag setting at creation
    82→- `mark_layer_local_only_if_needed()` — replaced by `unit.set_local_only()`
    83→
    84→**Keep methods**:
    85→- `should_sync_layer()` — still needed to compute `is_local_only` for new units
    86→- `can_write_layer()` — unchanged
    87→
    88→### ScribeArgs Changes
    89→
    90→- `layers: HashMap<String, Layer>` stays as-is (construction args)
    91→- `pre_start` converts args.layers → units
    92→
    93→### Cross-Cutting State (stays in ScribeState)
    94→
    95→These span all layers and remain in ScribeState:
    96→- `subscribers: Arc<RwLock<HashMap<...>>>` — per-peer, not per-layer
    97→- `page_update_subscribers: Arc<RwLock<Vec<...>>>` — page-level event bus
    98→- `pending_update_source: Arc<Mutex<Option<...>>>` — transient import context
    99→- `query_subscribers` — cross-layer queries
   100→- `sync_config`, `sync_event_tx` — page-level sync
   101→- `layer_storage`, `vector_storage`, `peer_resolver`, `permit_issuer` — storage traits
   102→- `our_permit`, `our_did` — page-level identity
   103→- `validation_handle`, `node_script_shutdown` — infrastructure
   104→
   105→### Observer Setup Changes
   106→
   107→**Key insight**: `is_local_only` is static per layer (determined at creation, never changes). The observer async task can capture it as a `bool` instead of cloning the shared `Arc<RwLock<HashSet>>`.
   108→
   109→Current (`loro_observer.rs:302-467`):
   110→```rust
   111→pub fn setup_layer_observer(state: &mut ScribeState, layer_name: &str) {
   112→    if state.loro_subscriptions.contains_key(layer_name) { return; }
   113→    let layer = state.layers.get(layer_name)?;
   114→    let local_only_for_task = state.local_only_layers.clone();  // Arc clone
   115→    // ...
   116→    state.loro_subscriptions.insert(layer_name, subscription);
   117→}
   118→```
   119→
   120→After:
   121→```rust
   122→pub fn setup_layer_observer(state: &mut ScribeState, layer_name: &str) {
   123→    let unit = state.units.get_mut(layer_name)?;
   124→    if unit.has_observer() { return; }
   125→
   126→    let layer_for_task = unit.layer().clone();
   127→    let is_local_only = unit.is_local_only();  // captured as bool
   128→    let subscribers_for_task = state.subscribers.clone();
   129→    let page_update_subscribers_for_task = state.page_update_subscribers.clone();
   130→    let pending_update_source = state.pending_update_source.clone();
   131→    let page_id_for_task = state.page_id.clone();
   132→
   133→    // Spawn async task — uses `is_local_only` bool instead of Arc<RwLock<HashSet>>
   134→    tokio::spawn(async move {
   135→        while let Some(signal) = signal_rx.recv().await {
   136→            // ... same logic, but:
   137→            if is_local_only { continue; }  // instead of: if local_only.read().contains(...)
   138→            // ...
   139→        }
   140→    });
   141→
   142→    let subscription = unit.layer().subscribe_root(move |diff_event| { ... });
   143→    unit.set_observer(subscription);
   144→}
   145→```
   146→
   147→### Operations Pattern Change
   148→
   149→Current (`operations.rs`):
   150→```rust
   151→fn ensure_layer_exists(state: &mut ScribeState, layer_name: &str) -> bool {
   152→    let is_new = !state.layers.contains_key(layer_name);
   153→    if is_new {
   154→        state.layers.insert(layer_name.to_string(), Layer::new());
   155→        state.mark_layer_local_only_if_needed(layer_name);
   156→    }
   157→    is_new
   158→}
   159→// ...
   160→let layer = state.layers.get(layer_name).unwrap();
   161→layer.list_push(path, &item)?;
   162→layer.commit();
   163→state.dirty_layers.insert(layer_name.to_string());
   164→```
   165→
   166→After:
   167→```rust
   168→fn ensure_layer_exists(state: &mut ScribeState, layer_name: &str) -> bool {
   169→    let is_new = !state.units.contains_key(layer_name);
   170→    if is_new {
   171→        let mut unit = LayerUnit::new_empty();
   172→        unit.set_local_only(!state.should_sync_layer(layer_name));
   173→        state.units.insert(layer_name.to_string(), unit);
   174→    }
   175→    is_new
   176→}
   177→// ...
   178→let unit = state.units.get_mut(layer_name).unwrap();
   179→unit.layer().list_push(path, &item)?;
   180→unit.layer().commit();
   181→unit.mark_dirty();
   182→```
   183→
   184→### Flush Change
   185→
   186→Current (`sync/mod.rs:91-115`):
   187→```rust
   188→for layer_name in state.dirty_layers.drain() {
   189→    if let Some(layer) = state.layers.get(&layer_name) {
   190→        let snapshot = layer.export_snapshot();
   191→        state.layer_storage.save_layer(&layer_name, &snapshot)?;
   192→    }
   193→}
   194→```
   195→
   196→After:
   197→```rust
   198→for (name, unit) in state.units.iter_mut() {
   199→    if let Some(snapshot) = unit.take_dirty_snapshot() {
   200→        if let Err(e) = state.layer_storage.save_layer(name, &snapshot) {
   201→            tracing::error!(layer = %name, error = %e, "Failed to save layer");
   202→        }
   203→    }
   204→}
   205→```
   206→
   207→### Reconciliation Change
   208→
   209→Current (`sync/reconcile.rs:33-60`):
   210→```rust
   211→for layer_name in state.layers.keys().cloned().collect::<Vec<_>>() {
   212→    let our_vector = match state.layers.get(&layer_name) { ... };
   213→```
   214→
   215→After:
   216→```rust
   217→for (layer_name, unit) in &state.units {
   218→    let our_vector = unit.layer().version_vector();
   219→```
   220→
   221→---
   222→
   223→## Files to Modify
   224→
   225→| File | Changes |
   226→|------|---------|
   227→| `scribe/src/layer_unit/mod.rs` | Add `LayerUnit` struct + impl |
   228→| `scribe/src/state.rs` | Replace 4 collections with `units`, remove `update_local_only_layers()` / `mark_layer_local_only_if_needed()` |
   229→| `scribe/src/actor.rs` | `pre_start`: build units from args.layers; all `handle` arms: use `state.units` |
   230→| `scribe/src/operations.rs` | `ensure_layer_exists` + all 6 handlers: use units |
   231→| `scribe/src/loro_observer.rs` | `setup_layer_observer` + `setup_observers_for_all_layers`: use units, capture `is_local_only` as bool |
   232→| `scribe/src/sync/mod.rs` | `handle_flush`, sync request handlers: use units |
   233→| `scribe/src/sync/apply.rs` | `UpdateContext::new`, `create_layer_from_peer`, `apply_crdt_update`, `update_sender_vector`, `handle_post_apply`: use units |
   234→| `scribe/src/sync/broadcast.rs` | `broadcast_update`, `notify_layer_discovered`: use units |
   235→| `scribe/src/sync/reconcile.rs` | `handle_reconcile_with_peers`: iterate units |
   236→| `scribe/src/sync/subscription.rs` | `send_initial_state_to_subscriber`: iterate units |
   237→| `scribe/src/query.rs` | `handle_query`: use units |
   238→| `scribe/src/permit.rs` | No changes (delegates to gurkha) |
   239→| `scribe/src/layer_unit/dynamic.rs` | Use `state.units` instead of `state.layers` |
   240→| `scribe/src/ephemeral.rs` | No changes (doesn't access layers) |
   241→
   242→## Mechanical Transformation Rules
   243→
   244→Every access site follows one of these patterns:
   245→
   246→| Before | After |
   247→|--------|-------|
   248→| `state.layers.get(name)` | `state.units.get(name).map(\|u\| u.layer())` |
   249→| `state.layers.get_mut(name)` | `state.units.get_mut(name).map(\|u\| u.layer())` |
   250→| `state.layers.contains_key(name)` | `state.units.contains_key(name)` |
   251→| `state.layers.insert(name, Layer::new())` | `state.units.insert(name, LayerUnit::new_empty())` |
   252→| `state.layers.insert(name, layer)` | `state.units.insert(name, LayerUnit::new(layer))` |
   253→| `state.layers.keys()` | `state.units.keys()` |
   254→| `state.layers.entry(name).or_insert_with(Layer::new)` | Unit entry pattern (see below) |
   255→| `state.dirty_layers.insert(name)` | `state.units.get_mut(name).unwrap().mark_dirty()` |
   256→| `state.dirty_layers.drain()` | iterate `units.iter_mut()`, check `take_dirty_snapshot()` |
   257→| `state.dirty_layers.is_empty()` | `state.units.values().all(\|u\| !u.is_dirty())` |
   258→| `state.dirty_layers.remove(name)` | `state.units.get_mut(name).map(\|u\| u.clear_dirty())` |
   259→| `state.loro_subscriptions.contains_key(name)` | `state.units.get(name).map(\|u\| u.has_observer()).unwrap_or(false)` |
