│
COORDINATOR
├─ Receive NewDynamicLayer event
│  └─ on_distribute_layer_permits()
│     └─ For each (recipient_did, permit_token):
│        ├─ Store in Butler (page_id/user_did/layer_name → token)
│        └─ Send to PeerActor (or queue if not connected)
│
PEER ACTOR (Viewer)
├─ Receive LayerPermit message
│  └─ on_layer_permit()
│     ├─ Store layer permit in Butler
│     └─ issue_layer_consent()
│        ├─ Parse layer permit to get issuer's DID
│        ├─ Issue consent permit via gurkha::issue_sync_layer_consent()
│        └─ Send LayerConsentGrant back to node
│
NODE (receiving consent)
├─ Receive LayerConsentGrant
│  └─ on_layer_consent_grant()
│     └─ Store viewer's consent in Butler
```

---

This flow is **fully operational for role-based explicit layers**. For **named participant explicit layers**, the missing piece is the participant enumeration and issuance logic in `prepare_layer_permits()`.

